# AI directive — master doc routing

## Documentation ideology

- **Product story / user acceptance first.** Prefer reading and updating the user-facing
  acceptance or product-story doc before implementation details or file-tree inventories.
- **Then the code.** Implementation follows the accepted behavior contract.
- **Thin system contracts only when needed** — security, money, ingest, critical E2E, or
  other high-risk seams the project already documents as contracts.
- **This file is the keyword router.** Match the user prompt to a row below (or a
  project-local override) and read those doc paths directly. Do not chain through other
  Cursor rules or sprawling "see also" trees for topic context.
- **Update existing docs first.** Prefer editing the canonical file for the topic before
  creating a new markdown file.
- **Add new docs only when necessary.** Create a new file when the topic is genuinely new,
  large, or owned by a separate subsystem and cannot fit cleanly in an existing canonical doc.
- **Avoid doc sprawl.** One source of truth per topic; cross-link briefly if needed.
- **Do not add new `alwaysApply` topic rules** for product/architecture policies. Put policy
  in the correct doc and extend the keyword map via a **non-colliding local override**
  (see `templates/doc-routing.local.example.mdc` in cursor-harness).

## Default documentation roots

| Area | Typical location | Scope |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Project overview | `README.md`, `AGENTS.md` | Orientation, commands, owners |
| Specs / architecture | `docs/`, `docs/specs/`, `docs/architecture/` | Feature and system contracts |
| Changelog / releases | `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/changelog.md` | Release notes |
| Project memory | `project_memory.md` | Bounded learning overlay (not SSOT) |

If the consumer project uses different roots, prefer those paths when discoverable from
`README.md` / `AGENTS.md` / a local doc-routing override.

## Default keyword table

Before starting any feature, bug fix, or optimization, identify the core topic and read the
mapped file(s). **Project-local overrides win** when present under `.cursor/rules/` with a
non-harness filename (e.g. `doc-routing.local.mdc`).

| If the prompt mentions… | Read first… | Focus |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Architecture overview, system overview, codebase map, how the app works | `README.md`, `docs/architecture/**`, `docs/**/overview*` | Whole-system mental model |
| Project memory, lessons learned, retrospective, Phase 7, `project_memory.md` | `project_memory.md`, `.cursor/skills/project-memory/SKILL.md` | Bounded learning overlay |
| Vision, goals, product north star | `docs/vision/**`, `README.md` | Product intent |
| Scope, new feature boundaries | `docs/specs/**`, `docs/scope*` | Supported vs unsupported |
| Tests, coverage, mocks, E2E | `docs/testing/**`, `testing` rule, CI config | Testing standards and gates |
| Deploy, CI/CD, production, release | `docs/deployment/**`, `.github/workflows/**`, `README.md` | Ship workflow |
| Environment variables, secrets, `.env` | `docs/**/environment*`, `*.env.example`, `README.md` | Env SSOT and rotation |
| Backend / API | `docs/backend/**`, `docs/api/**`, OpenAPI/spec files | Server contracts |
| Frontend / UI | `docs/frontend/**`, design docs | UI structure |
| Database / schema / migrations | `docs/database/**`, migration folder README | Schema workflow |
| Backlog, tech debt, future work | `docs/backlog.md`, issue tracker links in README | Deferred work |
| Changelog, versioning, SemVer | `CHANGELOG.md`, versioning docs | Release impact |
| Ship local, merge to main, worktree cleanup | `.cursor/skills/ship-local/SKILL.md` | Local merge protocol |
| Ship prod, watched CI, deploy, Phase 7 | `.cursor/skills/workflows/ship-prod/SKILL.md`, `docs/deployment/**` | Remote ship + CI |
| Candidates, cycle status, staged harness promote | `project_memory.md`, `.cursor/skills/project-memory/SKILL.md` | Scored memory ladder |

When no row matches: search under `docs/` (and README) for the closest SSOT; read that file
only. Do not invent parallel documentation.

## Spec updates

Update docs in the **same area** you changed before considering the task complete.

| You changed… | Update… |
| :--- | :--- |
| Feature behavior / API / UX contract | Matching product-story / acceptance / `docs/specs/` file |
| System structure, data flow, boundaries | Matching file under `docs/architecture/` or equivalent |
| Public release-facing behavior | `CHANGELOG.md` (or project changelog) when the project uses one |
| Agent lifecycle / memory skill schema | `project_memory.md` scaffold notes if the format changes |
| Harness packs (skills/rules/agents/workflows) | `.cursor/HARNESS.md` in the same change |

If no canonical doc exists and the change is material, create the smallest necessary doc in
the project's existing docs layout — do not invent a new top-level docs tree.
